G5207.def:
**υἱός**, -οῦ, ὁ, [in LXX very frequently and nearly always for בֵּן, [[Gen.4.17|Gen.4:17]], al.; for בַּר, [[Dan.7.13|Dan LXX TH 7:13]], al.; etc. ;],
**a son**;
1. **in the ordinary sense**: [[Mat.10.37|Mat.10:37]], [[Mrk.9.17|Mrk.9:17]], [[Luk.1.13|Luk.1:13]], al. mult.; omitted with the art. of origin (WM, §30, 3; Bl., §35, 2), τὸν τοῦ Ἰεσσαί, [[Act.13.22|Act.13:22]] (LXX); also with genitive anarth. (cl.), Σώπατρος Πύρρου Βεροιαῖος, [[Act.20.4|Act.20:4]] with adj., προτότοκος, [[Luk.2.7|Luk.2:7]] μονογένης, [[Luk.7.12|Luk.7:12]] opposite to νόθος, [[Heb.12.8|Heb.12:8]] in a wider sense, of posterity: ὁ υἱ. Δαυΐδ, of the Messiah (cf. Dalman, _Words_, 316ff.; _DCG_, ii, 653f.), [[Mat.22.42, 45|Mat.22:42, 45]] [[Mrk.12.35, 37|Mrk.12:35, 37]] [[Luk.20.41, 44|Luk.20:41, 44]] al.; υἱοὶ Ἰσραήλ, (cf. υἷες Ἀχαιῶν, Hom., _Il._, i, 162, al.), [[Mat.27.9|Mat.27:9]], [[Act.9.15|Act.9:15]], al.
2. Metaphorical;
(a) **as belonging to, being connected with or having the quality of that which follows **(a usage mainly due to translation from a Semitic original; cf. Deiss., _BS_, 161ff.; Dalman, _Words_, 115f.; _DCG_, ii, 652f.): τ. πονεροῦ (διαβόλου), [[Mat.13.38|Mat.13:38]], [[Act.13.10|Act.13:10]]; τ. νυμφῶνος (see: νυμφών), [[Mat.9.15|Mat.9:15]], [[Mrk.2.19|Mrk.2:19]], al.; τ. φωτός (Lft., _Notes_, 74), [[Luk.16.8|Luk.16:8]], [[Jhn.12.36|Jhn.12:36]], [[1Th.5.5|1Th.5:5]]; τ. εἰρεήμης, [[Luk.10.6|Luk.10:6]] γεέννης, [[Mat.23.15|Mat.23:15]] τ. ἀπωλείας, [[Jhn.17.12|Jhn.17:12]], [[2Th.2.3|2Th.2:3]]; τ. αἰῶνος τούτου, [[Luk.16.8; 20.34|Luk.16:8 20:34]]; τ. ἀπειθειάς, [[Eph.2.2; 5.6|Eph.2:2 5:6]]; βροντῆς, [[Mrk.3.17|Mrk.3:17]] τ. ἀναστάσεως, [[Luk.20.36|Luk.20:36]] παρακλήσεως, [[Act.4.36|Act.4:36]] τ. προφητῶν κ. τ. διαθήκης, [[Act.3.25|Act.3:25]]
(b) υἱὸς τ. θεοῦ (cf. Dalman, _Words_, 268ff.; Deiss., _BS_, 166f.; _DB_, iv, 570 ff.; _DCG_, ii, 654ff.), of men, as partakers of the Divine nature and of the life to come: [[Mat.5.9|Mat.5:9]], [[Luk.20.36|Luk.20:36]], [[Rom.8.14; 9.26|Rom.8:14 9:26]], al.; υἱοὶ (κ. θυγατέρες) τ. ὑψίστου, [[Luk.6.35|Luk.6:35]], [[2Co.6.18|2Co.6:18]]; in an unique sense of Jesus, [[Mat.4.3; 8.29; 28.19|Mat.4:3 8:29 28:19]], [[Mrk.3.4|Mrk.3:4]], [[Luk.4.41|Luk.4:41]], [[Jhn.9.35; 11.27|Jhn.9:35 11:27]], al.; ὁ Χριστὸς ὁ υἱ. τ. θεοῦ ζῶντος (τ. εὐλογητοῦ), [[Mat.16.16|Mat.16:16]], [[Mrk.14.61|Mrk.14:61]];
(with) (ὁ) υἱὸς τοῦ ἀνθρώπου (in LXX for Heb. בּן אדם, Aram, בּר אנשׁ; cf. Dalman, _Words_, 234ff.; _DB_, iv, 579ff.; _DCG_, ii, 659ff.; Westc., _St. John_, i, 74ff.; other reff. in Swete, _Mk_, 2:10), based on the Aram. of [[Dan.7.13|Dan.7:13]], where the phrase, like the corresponding Heb. (as in [[Psa.8.5|Psa.8:5]]), means **a man**, one of the species, and indicates the human appearance of the person in question. It is used of the Messiah in Enoch, with 46, §1-4, also in II [[Est.13.3, 12|Est.13:3, 12]], al. Our Lord first makes the phrase a title, using the def. art. It seems to combine the ideas of his true humanity and representative character. Exc. in [[Act.7.56|Act.7:56]] and (anarth.) [[Rev.1.13|Rev.1:13]] [[Rev.14.14|14:14]], it is used of Jesus only by himself: [[Mat.8.20|Mat.8:20]], [[Mrk.2.10|Mrk.2:10]], [[Luk.5.24|Luk.5:24]], [[Jhn.1.52|Jhn.1:52]], al.
(AS)

G5244.def:
**ὑπερήφανος**, -ον
(ὑπέρ, φαίνομαι, with η pleonast., see Kühner3, I, 189) [in LXX for זֵד, גֵּאֶה, לוּץ, etc. ;]
**showing oneself above others**;
(a) in good sense (Plat., al.), pre-eminent, splendid;
(b) more frequently in had sense, and so always in Scr., **arrogant, haughty, disdainful **(see Westc. _Epp. Jo._, 65b): [[Rom.1.30|Rom.1:30]], [[2Ti.3.2|2Ti.3:2]]; διανοίᾳ καρδίας, [[Luk.1.51|Luk.1:51]] opposite to ταπεινός (as in [[Pro.3.34|Pro.3:34]]), [[Jas.4.6|Jas.4:6]], [[1Pe.5.5|1Pe.5:5]]" (LXX) .†
_SYN._: ἀλαζών, ὑβριστής, see Tr., _Syn._, § xxix (AS)

G5215.def:
**ὕμνος**, -ου, ὁ
[in LXX for תְּהִלָּה, נְגִינָה, שִׁיר, etc. ;]
**a hymn**;
(a) in cl. a festal song in praise of gods or heroes;
(b) **in LXX and NT a song of praise addressed to God**: [[Eph.5.19|Eph.5:19]], [[Col.3.16|Col.3:16]].†
_SYN._: ψαλμός, that which is sung to a musical accompaniment; ᾠδή, the generic term for song (cf. Tr., _Syn._, § LXXviii, Lft. on [[Col.3.16|Col.3:16]]) (AS)
